Here is a single ready-to-deploy hardening plan for VAZQZ: make the repo explicitly ESM, add a Node 18+ engine floor, clean up the LSP import path, remove global prototype mutation, and make registry/path handling safer �.
Deploy-ready patch set
package.json
Add or ensure:
{
  "type": "module",
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=18.0.0"
  }
}
This makes the runtime model explicit and keeps deployment expectations clear �.
src/cli.ts
Use the simpler output path rewrite:
const outFile = fullPath.replace(".vz", ".wat");
That avoids regex escaping issues and is stable for your current compiler flow.
src/pm/manager.ts
Use ESM imports only:
import fs from "fs";
import path from "path";
import os from "os";
import { execSync } from "child_process";
import https from "https";
import { createHash } from "crypto";
import chalk from "chalk";
Remove all require(...) usage, and if tar is optional, guard it and show a clear install error instead of failing mid-command �.
src/pm/registry.ts
Replace regex-heavy pathname matching with segment-based logic:
const parts = pathname.split("/").filter(Boolean);
const isPackage = parts.length === 1;
const isTarball = parts.length === 3 && parts[1] === "-" && parts[2].endsWith(".tgz");
That is more robust than relying on fragile escape-heavy regexes.
src/lsp/server.ts
Remove any String.prototype extensions entirely and use standalone helpers:
function lastIndexOfAny(str: string, chars: string, fromIndex?: number): number {
  const start = fromIndex ?? str.length - 1;
  for (let i = start; i >= 0; i--) if (chars.includes(str[i])) return i;
  return -1;
}

function indexOfAny(str: string, chars: string, fromIndex?: number): number {
  const start = fromIndex ?? 0;
  for (let i = start; i < str.length; i++) if (chars.includes(str[i])) return i;
  return -1;
}
Also prefer vscode-languageserver/node if that is the package entry your resolver actually expects �.
Extra robustness
Add a startup check for missing optional dependencies like tar, and fail with a helpful message.
Wrap registry request parsing in try/catch and return JSON errors consistently.
Normalize all file paths with path.resolve() before reading or writing outputs.
Keep run, compile, and wasm deterministic by writing sidecar output next to the input source file only.
Final deploy order
Apply the file edits above.
Run npm install.
Run npm run build.
Test run, compile, wasm, and init.
Package vazqz-lang-FINAL.zip.
Tag and release v0.9.1 �.
